{:mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YK7FyrZdXGwwklx8UKaEZbWmnu5Cg", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YK7FyrZdXGwwklx8UKaEZbWmnu5Cg", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YK7Fzo6dtxqFEYQ7t7JvWYowikalD", :mulog/timestamp 1779242173687, :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/anomaly-in-todo-processor, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :anomaly {:cognitect.anomalies/category :cognitect.anomalies/fault, :cognitect.anomalies/message "Todo Processor returned nil: %s"}}
{:mulog/duration 69791, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :event {:tick-id #uuid "949f7490-3e63-4ab2-a805-026ed32efc9b", :writes {:document-survey "### Document Structure Survey: microFIT Contract Evolution (v2.0 vs v3.1.1)\n\n#### 1. General Layout and High-Level Structure\nBoth `contract_v2` and `contract_v3` follow a nearly identical modular architecture, consisting of two primary parts followed by a series of technical appendices. \n\n*   **Part 1: Contract Details** – Focuses on project-specific data (Supplier info, Facility specs).\n*   **Part 2: General Terms and Conditions** – Focuses on the legal framework, covenants, and administrative rules.\n*   **Appendices (A through E)** – Specialized definitions and technology/connection specific rules.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Sectional Review\n\n**Part 1 – Contract Details**\n*   **A. Contract and Supplier Information:** Captures Reference Numbers, ID dates, LDC account details, and the Contract Price.\n*   **B. Facility Characteristics:** Technical specs including Renewable Fuel type, Nameplate Capacity, and Connection types (Direct/Indirect/Parallel).\n*   **C. Documents Included:** A checklist identifying which appendices are legally active for the specific project.\n\n**Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions**\n1.  **Term:** Defines the duration.\n2.  **Pricing and Payment:** Mechanisms for Indexed Contract Prices and LDC settlement cycles.\n3.  **Environmental Attributes:** Directs the transfer of rights/credits to the OPA.\n4.  **Representations and Warranties:** Supplier assertions regarding eligibility, metering, and legality.\n5.  **Covenants:** Ongoing obligations (no capacity increases, maintaining eligibility).\n6.  **General Conditions:** Audit rights, FIPPA (Freedom of Information) compliance, and information disclosure consents.\n7.  **Notices:** Procedures for official communication.\n8.  **Termination:** Conditions for ending the agreement (Notice, Breach, or Automatic).\n9.  **Amendment / 10. Assignment:** Rules for modifying or transferring the contract.\n11. **Governing Law / 12. Dispute Resolution:** Legal jurisdiction (Ontario) and arbitration procedures.\n13. **LDC Failure to Pay:** OPA guarantee of payments.\n14. **Multiple Entities:** Joint and several liability clauses.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Appendix Survey\n*   **Appendix A (Definitions):** Alphabetical glossary of terms.\n*   **Appendix B (Indexed Price):** Mathematical formula for CPI-based price adjustments.\n*   **Appendix C (Solar PV Schedule):** \n    *   *v2.0 version:* Contains extensive \"Domestic Content\" tables/grids (Crystalline, Thin-Film, Concentrated) requiring 60% local sourcing.\n    *   *v3.1.1 version:* Significantly simplified; the detailed grids and the \"Minimum Required Domestic Content\" requirements found in v2.0 are removed.\n*   **Appendix D-1 & D-2:** Technical schedules for Direct vs. Indirect connections and battery back-up configurations.\n*   **Appendix E (LDC Schedule):** Modifications for instances where the LDC is the Supplier.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Key Structural Transitions (v2 to v3)\n*   **Removal of Domestic Content:** The most significant structural change is in **Appendix C**. v2.0 includes a comprehensive regulatory framework for Ontario-based manufacturing/labor scoring. v3.1.1 removes these tables entirely.\n*   **Prescribed Forms:** v3.1.1 introduces the concept of the \"Prescribed Form\" (found in Sections 5.1.2, 7.2, 8.1, and 9). This indicates a move toward standardized, web-based administrative templates rather than open-ended written notice.\n*   **Enhanced Disclosure:** Section 6.5 in v3.1.1 adds specific language regarding disclosure for \"public health and safety\" and \"emergency services,\" which was absent in v2.0.\n*   **Website Integration:** v3.1.1 formally defines and integrates the \"Website\" as a source for the latest forms and rules."}, :duration-ms 7108, :event/tags #{[:node #uuid "12630c00-eb68-4473-9399-d6517e2f7956"] [:sheet #uuid "74303876-0ee3-4ad2-9076-81cf7a129476"] [:tick #uuid "949f7490-3e63-4ab2-a805-026ed32efc9b"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T20:56:13.685454-05:00", :usage {:prompt-tokens 25420, :completion-tokens 892, :total-tokens 26312}, :status :success, :node-id #uuid "12630c00-eb68-4473-9399-d6517e2f7956", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-completed, :sheet-id #uuid "74303876-0ee3-4ad2-9076-81cf7a129476", :event/id #uuid "019e4319-04f5-701d-bc7c-91b4dfc1032c"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YK7FyrZdXGwwklx8UKaEZbWmnu5Cg", :mulog/timestamp 1779242173687, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YK7FyrZdXGwwklx8UKaEZbWmnu5Cg", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
