ement for \"Prescribed Forms\" (Sections 5, 7, 8, 9) favors the OPA’s internal processing and data management, ensuring that notices of termination or amendment are uniform and legally robust.\n    *   **Public Safety Disclosure:** The new provision in Section 6.5 reduces liability for the OPA when sharing data with emergency services, clarifying their right to act in the interest of public safety.\n\n### 3. Key Legal & Operational Impacts\n*   **Procurement Strategy:** Suppliers can now optimize for price and technology rather than geographic origin.\n*   **Notice Compliance:** The introduction of the \"Prescribed Form\" definition means that informal notices (e.g., a standard letter or email) may no longer be contractually valid for major actions like termination or amendments, requiring stricter adherence to OPA’s web-based templates.\n*   **Confidentiality:** There is a slight narrowing of privacy as the OPA expands its right to disclose facility details to government agencies for emergency planning, though this is a standard regulatory evolution.\n\n**Conclusion:** The transition to Version 3.1.1 represents a **deregulatory shift** that primarily benefits the Supplier by removing protectionist trade requirements and offering more flexible eligibility pathways, while standardizing administrative interactions through prescribed digital forms."}, :duration-ms 4713, :event/tags #{[:node #uuid "3fe0c114-3d94-4ed5-bea2-589c6ff6de48"] [:sheet #uuid "74303876-0ee3-4ad2-9076-81cf7a129476"] [:tick #uuid "949f7490-3e63-4ab2-a805-026ed32efc9b"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T20:56:28.006881-05:00", :usage {:prompt-tokens 1512, :completion-tokens 640, :total-tokens 2152}, :status :success, :node-id #uuid "3fe0c114-3d94-4ed5-bea2-589c6ff6de48", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-completed, :sheet-id #uuid "74303876-0ee3-4ad2-9076-81cf7a129476", :event/id #uuid "019e4319-3ce6-70a2-8498-9040cb34abf1"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YKxcNKKmXqSvu4yRkq